# 21 — Measure sensor-feature forecasting utility

**Goal / what to deliver:** Determine whether supported causal LiDAR/camera-token scene features improve forecasting beyond tracks/maps.

**Blocked by:** [20](20-motion-baseline.md)

**Status:** planned — blocked by prerequisite verification

**Lane:** core

**Verifier:** Live matched retraining of no-extra-evidence adapter control, LiDAR and camera-token treatments; independent feature-time/missingness audit and scenario-paired metric analysis.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Declare compatible feature source/encoder adapter; Perception SAM artifacts are not assumed to join Motion.
- [ ] Hold eligible scenarios, decoder/interface capacity, K/horizon, seeds and optimization budget fixed; report full-cohort extension coverage.
- [ ] Primary mAP effects and 95% scenario-level intervals, complementary metrics/probability diagnostics and total feature cost are reported.
- [ ] A frozen-head probe is separate and only used with a compatible trained interface.
- [ ] Promotion requires positive lower interval bound for primary improvement under the frozen resource cap; null/negative findings remain valid completion.
- [ ] Independently validate live Insula receipt, candidate/input/runtime identities, required assertions, output hashes and measured resources; missing or failed checks prohibit closure.
- [ ] Publish a reviewable evidence summary with exact replay recipe, observed outcome and limitations; existing host tests or historical receipts alone do not close this ticket.

## Binding completion policy

[Program goal and evidence policy](program-goal.md) applies in full. Preparation may occur before blockers clear; candidate execution/promotion and completion require verified blockers. Scientific completion permits negative/inconclusive findings. Adoption requires the separately stated promotion rule.
